You have exposure keratopathy in one or both eyes. This means the surface of the eye is drying out because it is not being covered or protected well enough by the eyelids.\
\
This can happen if the eyes do not close fully during sleep, if blinking is incomplete, or if the eye surface is more exposed than usual. Symptoms can include dryness, burning, irritation, blur, and light sensitivity.\
